    <string name="info_title">How to connect your Kindle</string>
    <string name="info_step1">Turn the server on with the switch above and keep KoSend open while sending.</string>
    <string name="info_step2">On the Kindle, open KOReader and tap the top edge of the screen to show the menu. Open the wrench tab, choose Calibre, then Connect.</string>
    <string name="info_step3">The first time, KOReader asks which folder to save books in. Then it finds your phone and receives the queued books one after another. Books you add while connected are sent right away.</string>
    <string name="info_note_ip">Your phone and Kindle must be on the same Wi-Fi network. If the Kindle can’t find your phone, in KOReader open Calibre, then Wireless settings, and set Server address to Manual: IP %1$s, port %2$d.</string>
    <string name="info_note_noip">Your phone and Kindle must be on the same Wi-Fi network. If the Kindle can’t find your phone, you can enter the address manually in KOReader under Calibre, Wireless settings: it appears here while the server is on.</string>

